    "body": "## Summary\n- Preserve the scripted Oleg escape cap at five votes; the ordinary NPC-pool cutoff remains active for non-scripted escapes.\n- Keep Core as the sole owner of final vote outcomes. Persist each vote, its next deadline, and the separate outcome delay for reload/resume.\n- Keep the previously accepted Nastya random first-four order and fifth-player result, plus Oleg payment/recovery, boot routing, fresh-start REP baseline, and docs counterparts.\n- Add an actual Core timer-callback regression for NPC pool sizes 3 and 4, all six first-four permutations for both attempts, and an ordinary small-pool escape.\n\n## Validation\n- RED reproduced against the pre-fix Core: the real timer callback reached vote three, restored `pickDefense`, and removed the active vote.\n- GREEN: lifecycle/Core timer regression passes; the 12 scripted permutations retain 2:2 after vote four and settle to 2:3 failure or 3:2 success only after vote five. Ordinary pool-size-three escape still settles using the existing shortcut.\n- Targeted Stage 7.15 regressions, syntax checks, and `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- Core, Stage 7.15 controller, and index Web/docs pairs are byte-identical. `ui-boot.js` has broad pre-existing Web/docs drift from `origin/main`; the changed Stage 7.15 routing hunks are paired, and unrelated drift was preserved.\n\n## Native runtime\n- Full single-tab Codex Browser route previously completed on clean origins :8816 and :8817 using the same application source bytes: fresh start at 1 REP; Nastya 3:2; Oleg escape one 2:3 failure; escape two 3:2 success; individual visible vote states and 1-2 second intervals; reload/resume during votes and after settlement; exactly-once economy/messages; final instruction to start an independent dispute.\n- In this continuation, :8803 was found to contain an existing progressed save and was preserved. A fresh run on :8819 started through the UI and visibly showed 1 REP, but a later browser read was denied by Codex automatic review. No browser workaround was attempted. The current :8819 run is incomplete; the prior full runtime evidence remains the completed route for the same application bytes.\n\n## Status\n- Final head: `efdcfc641be250489aeb67291e11ce26c1d413a0`.\n- CI: `telemetry-receiver-checks` and `ai-forensics-evidence` SUCCESS.\n- PR remains draft and unmerged pending continued native-browser review. No Atom 7.",
